# Dev changelog

`DEV_CHANGELOG.md` (repo root) is the record of local work: which files changed on which date, why,
how to undo DB changes, local test data, and open items.

- At the start of a session, read `DEV_CHANGELOG.md` to recover context (setup steps, recent features, known issues).
- After changing files, add them under a dated heading `## YYYY-MM-DD — <feature>` with **New files** / **Modified files** lists and a one-line reason each. Use the date from the session timestamp.
- For every new Prisma migration, add an "Undo the DB part" SQL block (drop objects + delete the `_prisma_migrations` row).
- Record any test data inserted into the local DB and how to delete it.
- Move items out of "Known open items" when they are fixed.
